    "Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play.",
    "Maqam Bastanikar is effectively Jins Sikah followed by Maqam Saba. Its scale starts with the root Jins Sikah on the tonic, then Jins Saba on the 3rd degree, an overlapping Jins Hijaz on the 5th degree, and finally Jins Nikriz on the octave.",
    "Explore other maqamat in the Maqam Sikah Family.",
    "Watch a 1-minute sample Violin Taqsim in Maqam Bastanikar by Sami Abu Shumays."
  ],
  "text": "Maqam Bastanikar A member of the Maqam Sikah Family Maqam Index Pronunciation of Bastanikar Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play. Maqam Bastanikar is effectively Jins Sikah followed by Maqam Saba . Its scale starts with the root Jins Sikah on the tonic , then Jins Saba on the 3 rd degree, an overlapping Jins Hijaz on the 5 th degree, and finally Jins Nikriz on the octave. Explore other maqamat in the Maqam Sikah Family . Watch a 1-minute sample Violin Taqsim in Maqam Bastanikar by Sami Abu Shumays. Zalamu (1957) Abdel Halim Hafez Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Ahl el-Hawa (1958) Umm Kulthum Music by Zakariya Ahmad (Egypt) Inti Fakrani (1938) Umm Kulthum Music by Muhammad al-Qasabgi (Egypt) Muwashah Anshidi Ya Saba Palestininan National Arabic Orchestra Director Ramzi Abu Radwan Music by Yehiya al-Sa‘udi Muwashah Aqbala al-Subhu Yughanni Ensemble Ornina (Syria) Conductor Dr. Muhammad Qadri Dalal Music by Bakri al-Kurdi Muwashah Nara al-‘Iqda Ensemble Ornina (Syria) Conductor Dr. Muhammad Qadri Dalal Muwashah Nuzhatu al-Arwahi Badri (performer unknown) Taqsim Oud in Maqam Bastanikar Muhammad Qadri Dalal Maqamat Insolites Taqsim Oud in Maqam Sikah Riyad al-Sunbati Taqaseem Oud",
